    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="0652" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6704: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Leopoldville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mallon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leopoldville</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-17T14:00:00+01:00">November 17,
                            1940—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have been asked to accompany High Commissioner de Larminat on a visit by plane
                    to Libreville and Port Gentil to witness the effects of the recent bombs.
                    Departure set for early in the morning November 20. Respectfully request
                    Department’s advice in time to accept or decline.</p>
                <p>De Gaulle left for London today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mallon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
